-- Natural grain (t3): nat writes floor to the integer grid and the ceiling is 2^53 — the last contiguous integer of the double, past which integer arithmetic loses exactness. Twin of 135-natural-grain.bqn.
-- Row 0 holds 2^52: one multiply crosses the ceiling and clamps; the division after is exact. Row 2's 28/8 = 3.5 floors to 3 — naturals stay natural.
--! registry ../registries/135-natural-grain.reg
--! expect fuel = 1125899906842624 5 3

Alive , fuel *= 4
Alive , fuel /= 8
